## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design real-time routing with SLAs, failure handling, and observability in a multi-tenant LLM-ops setup.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant SLO management and tail latency
- Health checks, circuit breakers, and backpressure
- Multi-backend routing with graceful degradation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo routing skeleton
function routePrompt(req){
  const tenant = req.tenantId;
  const candidateBackends = pickBackends(tenant);
  if(!backendAvailable(candidateBackends)) return fallbackParaphrase(req);
  const target = selectHealthyBackend(candidateBackends, tenant);
  return forward(req, target);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model drift in per-tenant SLOs and adapt routing?
- How would you test for extreme tail latency and ensure deterministic fallbacks?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to architect a real-time, multi-tenant streaming gateway with strict delivery guarantees, policy enforcement, and resilience under failure scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time streaming and exactly-once processing
- Per-tenant policy evaluation and data locality
- Backpressure, circuit breakers, and fault isolation
- Multi-variant routing (base, tuned, safety-guarded)
